1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,600
It's 6 AM. Summit Auto Group
runs 24 dealerships,

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:07,600
with 3,000 cars on the lots
and 9,000 open leads.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,800
In this sample,
652 leads are cold.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,800
Which customer should
each store call first?

5
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:18,300
SalesDesk.
Sell more: your AI sales analyst.

6
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:21,800
It works every lead,
at every rooftop, every night.

7
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:25,000
Here's tonight's review.

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,500
SalesDesk fans the work out
across all 24 rooftops:

9
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:31,800
six isolated workers
running in parallel on Vultr.

10
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:36,800
Each one checks every lead's risk
and searches the inventory

11
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:39,300
at its own store
and nearby sister stores.

12
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:42,500
Then Qwen on Vultr Inference
writes that store's brief.

13
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:50,800
By morning: 1,050 leads at risk,
1,007 matched to a car in stock,

14
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:54,800
and 792 distinct
aged units matched.

15
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,500
That's an estimated $3.4 million
in recoverable gross.

16
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:05,700
Leadership sees the group.
Every store manager gets a queue.

17
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:09,000
Let's open Sandy.

18
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:13,500
Forty follow-ups, ranked by risk
and by what's on the lot.

19
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:18,800
Maria asked about a blue
2024 RAV4 Hybrid nine days ago.

20
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:25,000
Her last contact was a week ago,
and the car she wanted sold.

21
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:28,000
Without a fresh match,
she needs another search.

22
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:33,500
SalesDesk found a silver one on this lot:
same model, same trim, in budget.

23
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:39,500
It has sat for 74 days,
with an entered daily carrying-cost assumption.

24
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:44,000
It knows she has
a 2017 CR-V to trade in.

25
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:51,500
And Qwen drafts the text
using only this car's recorded facts.

26
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:58,300
The manager reads, edits if needed,
and approves Sandy in one click.

27
00:01:58,300 --> 00:02:05,000
Vultr prepares the drafts, CRM tasks
and sister-store transfer requests.

28
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:09,500
These are drafts and tasks.
SalesDesk never sends customer messages.

29
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:17,300
Then close the laptop.
The next review runs at 2 AM,

30
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:20,300
every night, for every store,
on Vultr.

31
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:23,500
Tomorrow, the queue
is waiting again.

32
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:29,300
Before: managers dig through leads,
sold units and other stores' stock.

33
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:33,300
After: they approve
a ranked list.

34
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:37,300
The full 24-store review
ran in about two minutes twenty seconds.

35
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:43,300
Under the hood: a durable scheduler
on a Vultr VM,

36
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:47,300
a disposable Docker sandbox
for every rooftop,

37
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:52,000
and Qwen on Vultr Serverless Inference
for under one cent a run.

38
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:55,500
Automotive is our first vertical.

39
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:59,500
SalesDesk: sell more,
with your AI sales analyst.
